# Datasets (downloaded on first run; checksum-verified but bulky)
data/
*.gz
*.tar.gz

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Experiment outputs
# runs/ is TRACKED, deliberately: it holds every memo and every artifact the
# claim ledger cites. A ledger row whose evidence lives outside the repository
# is a citation that cannot be checked out. The model weights stay out — those
# are reproducible from the recorded configs.
#
# `checkpoints/` ALONE DID NOT DO THAT JOB. It matches only a top-level
# directory, and every checkpoint this program actually writes lives under
# `runs/ckpt_<arm>_seed<s>/mafc_seed<s>[_fp32]/task<k>_epoch<e>.pt`. So 76
# weight files totalling 1.22 GB were tracked while this file claimed they were
# excluded, and GitHub rejected the push on five of them (161-181 MB each,
# against a 100 MB limit). The pattern now names the path that exists, and
# `*.pt` backs it up so a future arm in a new directory cannot slip through.
runs_*/
checkpoints/
runs/ckpt_*/
*.pt
*.pth
*.json.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Datasets supplied locally (bulky; provenance recorded in runs/e5/FROZEN_CONFIG.json)
human+activity+recognition+using+smartphones.zip
*.zip
